{"id": "EUVD-2026-67561", "enisaUuid": "615265d8-ca5e-3d03-aaeb-fa4ec278096d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmm/util: don't read __page_2 for order-1 folios in snapshot_page()\n\nsnapshot_page() currently reads __page_2 after checking nr_pages > 1, but\nit should only do so when nr_pages > 2.\n\nIf an order-1 folio is allocated at the end of a vmemmap section,\n__page_2 will not exist and reading it will cause a fault.\n\nDuring DLPAR memory remove on a 22 TB ppc64le LPAR, snapshot_page() oopsed\non the page isolation path while reading an order-1 folio's __page_2 from\nan adjacent absent section (unmapped vmemmap).\n\nFix this to avoid reading memmap that doesn't exist (e.g., a vmemmap\nhole).", "datePublished": "2026-08-28T06:52:51", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-21T13:14:10", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9668ffe0e2a5e2399dce281620198a2e415871fc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c649324571206a30949765320b91ccdb4c1722dc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7441d6348c70738e9ed307510db171c7a9b3f4bf"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80685", "GHSA-ccm4-344c-hjv9"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02620000-d42c-3f88-868e-5b72e9dbae8b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "31a31da8a6187f1e5448ec73222e01d7d3fed4aa <7441d6348c70738e9ed307510db171c7a9b3f4bf"}, {"id": "06d9ecac-c468-39dd-a1a1-d5d52fad4502", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "31a31da8a6187f1e5448ec73222e01d7d3fed4aa <c649324571206a30949765320b91ccdb4c1722dc"}, {"id": "7b496229-7575-3c07-8645-6b73dc3762a7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.44"}, {"id": "87eadf92-fa42-3f1e-afd7-c4590e309e13", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.15"}, {"id": "ac9caa1a-e496-3d5f-8582-e9f4e38def47", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4117738bd42c8ab58090729daf0f8472a936f662"}, {"id": "b269813c-df37-3d2e-a595-9fd08a743070", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "31a31da8a6187f1e5448ec73222e01d7d3fed4aa <9668ffe0e2a5e2399dce281620198a2e415871fc"}, {"id": "bd23d958-29b6-3357-ad73-2ae169698088", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "be08d073-53c9-3627-974a-87c610c36b02", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.111 <6.13"}, {"id": "c5ad1d51-c6eb-39f3-b115-d17c712d4081", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "f2232601-d561-33e7-93a3-696f2c95229d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8f3bbe7b-cd90-35e2-a945-b3a9f16a0942", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}